<!DOCTYPE softwarelist SYSTEM "softwarelist.dtd">
<!--
license:CC0-1.0

    Roland SRX wave expansion boards, 32 MB each and word-wide, for the
    XV-3080, the XV-5080 and their relatives.  The board carries its own
    label in the clear at offset 0 of the scrambled image, "Roland SRX  "
    and then the magic 4F B0 58 A7 and the sixteen-byte identity the host
    compares, and the socket undoes eighteen permuted address lines within
    each 256 KB block and the eight data lines.

    Each entry is commented with that identity, with the name the machine
    shows, with the build date the board stamps ten bytes after it and with
    what the board's own directory at descrambled 0x40 declares, all read
    from the descrambled image.  The year is that build date, which is what
    the images testify to rather than the date of sale.

    The twelve parents are board reads.  Each declares its own board number
    as the identity word of that directory and carries a wave list, a sample
    list and one to four patch banks, and a host takes those patches.

    The clones are Roland's own plugin sets, which carry the wave data
    already descrambled, put back into board form by the inverse of the
    socket's permutation.  They are not the board and do not stand for it:
    each declares an identity from 0x1f up instead of its board number and
    carries no patch bank, so a host plays their waves and finds no patches
    on them.  They are what Roland ships, reproduced exactly.  Three of the
    plugin sets are not here because they need no entry of their own:
    SRX-02, SRX-10 and SRX-11's are their boards, byte for byte.  Of the
    rest, SRX-03's, SRX-04's and SRX-12's are the board's own sample data
    with the patch banks cut away; the other five are laid out afresh and
    carry fewer waves than the board does.

    Which board each PG-SRX re-issue is, is read off its waves: every wave
    of PG-SRX Orchestra, World, Strings and Classic EP stands in SRX-06,
    -09, -04 and -12, and 599 of PG-SRX Keyboards' 619 in SRX-07, where no
    other board shares more than three.
-->

